# Planning V2 renderer revision policy

Actual author: `/root`, 2026-10-10 UTC. This policy is frozen before the next producer source and candidate execution. It records a conservative production choice for the existing V2 contract. The seven public V2 specifications, exact manifest interface version, semantic rules, cohort coverage, search, novelty and split requirements remain unchanged.

The completed first V2 candidate remains immutable. Its actual whole-cohort audit reports 11 D-family renderer UNKNOWN errors. Separate input-derived expert and adversarial reviews find its targets and supplied witnesses/controls correct. The independently authored checker uses preservation of the order of shared goal-map keys as a sufficient renderer identification rule; the public contract does not explicitly specify that ordering under goal extension. See `reviews/oracle/RGM-v2-renderer-public-contract-assessment-20261010T062719Z.md` and its bound execution receipt. Independent adjudication of that original candidate remains separate.

For a fresh renderer revision, build a private presentation copy of each block task and sort its `goal_on` keys lexicographically before applying the existing two renderer transformations. The forward transformation preserves the chosen presentation order; the reverse transformation reverses the same presentation's object-key orders. Both transformations preserve action sequence order and every semantic value. Existing top-level, on-map and action-object rendering conventions remain unchanged. Sorting a map must never reorder the plan, change a goal constraint, add a metadata field to the student payload or change a target. The semantic task object and computed gold target keep their original meanings.

This ensures that adding goal constraints preserves the relative order of previously present keys in each renderer. Both styles must still be distinguishable from actual payload presentation, and every semantic control requires its own truthful declaration for each style. Test the change on partial-goal extension and valid detours, as well as the full unchanged checker. Do not omit a failing field from the checker or lower any existing coverage requirement.

Use a fresh generator version, fresh source freeze and separate artifact paths. Suggested production revision is `planning-gap-v2-renderer-r1` with generator version `rgm-planning-gap-2.0.3`. Its family manifest retains the public semantic cohort's required `batch_name="planning-gap-v2"`, `version="rgm-planning-controls-2.0.0"`, seven specification bindings and original V1 parent binding. Its fresh production revision and this policy hash belong in separate custody/reproducibility metadata. These production filenames and optional custody fields are not a new acceptance criterion. All old source attempts, original candidate/manifest, failed audits, first predictions and final judgments must remain byte-for-byte preserved.

A presentation revision of these same 408 rows contains zero new semantic tasks and zero new source families. State that reuse explicitly. Later reviewers may reuse their own frozen parent predictions only after proving exact input semantics and targets; disclose prior canonical exposure and the reused evidence. New rendered bytes, hashes, manifests, controls and publication eligibility require fresh review. Do not call that review an unseen blind semantic review. An actual independent adjudicator remains responsible for decisions, and a release still requires all deterministic gates plus the exact independent role actors.

No candidate is approved by this document. No training, sealed evaluation, GPU run or efficacy claim is authorized.
